<title>USA: U.S. Spring/White Wheat - Mill demand aids basis.</title>
<headline>U.S. Spring/White Wheat - Mill demand aids basis.</headline>
<dateline>CHICAGO 1996-10-15</dateline>
<text>
<p>Dark Northern Spring wheat cash basis bids were mostly stronger on Tuesday, boosted by mill demand and slow farmer selling.</p>
<p>The increase led to a rise in flat prices at many locations despite a lower close in MGE spring wheat futures.</p>
<p>&quot;The basis was up a nickel but the board was down so one largely offset the other. There is pretty good mill demand,&quot; one Minnesota based merchandiser said. The flat price in Minneapolis rose by one cent to $4.88 a bushel.</p>
<p>&quot;Nobody is selling,&quot; a Montana merchandiser said.</p>
<p>MGE Dec wheat ended off 4-1/4 cents at $4.17-3/4 a bushel.  </p>
